{
  "version": 1,
  "loadable": "cal",
  "reference": "util-linux 2.41 cal, built from the kernel.org release tarball (configure --disable-all-programs --enable-cal) because the reference host has no cal; its stdout under LC_ALL=C TZ=UTC is recorded as each contract's expected stdout. No expected value is taken from bash-os output. The runner's reference PATH has no cal, so these are contracts.",
  "coverage": [
    "G69: -w week numbers in util-linux's horizontal layout, US (Sunday) and ISO 8601 (-m) numbering, Julian cells, the 1752 reform, three-month spans and whole years, bundled short options; invalid months and years exit 1."
  ],
  "exclusions": [
    "bash-os keeps BSD (ncal -C) output for modes without -w; util-linux's non-week layout differs and is not claimed.",
    "Current-month output depends on the clock and is not checked."
  ],
